1
00:00:02,001 --> 00:00:03,669
PENNY:
Previously on The Big Bang Theory:

2
00:00:03,836 --> 00:00:07,339
-This is just a minor setback.
-No, it's not, okay?

3
00:00:07,507 --> 00:00:08,841
I've been out here for,
like, ten years.

4
00:00:09,008 --> 00:00:12,052
-I have nothing to show for it.
-Well, you have me.

5
00:00:14,305 --> 00:00:15,723
I do have you.

6
00:00:16,766 --> 00:00:18,392
Mmm.

7
00:00:22,271 --> 00:00:24,106
Leonard Hofstadter,

8
00:00:24,273 --> 00:00:25,857
will you marry me?

9
00:00:27,068 --> 00:00:28,694
Um...

10
00:00:31,030 --> 00:00:33,365
Did you seriously just say...umm?

11
00:00:34,992 --> 00:00:37,119
-It's an outrage.
- I know.

12
00:00:37,286 --> 00:00:39,454
The university, they think
they can do whatever they want.

13
00:00:39,622 --> 00:00:41,123
We just have to sit
there and take it.

14
00:00:41,290 --> 00:00:42,457
You need to let it go, Sheldon.

15
00:00:42,625 --> 00:00:45,294
You work tirelessly for someone
and this is what you get.

16
00:00:45,461 --> 00:00:49,256
Oh, my God! They're just making
you use your vacation days!

17
00:00:50,967 --> 00:00:52,259
But I don't want a vacation.

18
00:00:52,426 --> 00:00:55,220
Okay, listen, I don't mean to
diminish what you're going through,

19
00:00:55,388 --> 00:00:57,139
but I'm a little
distracted right now.

20
00:00:57,306 --> 00:00:58,974
Oh, this again?

21
00:00:59,141 --> 00:01:01,434
So, Penny proposed,
you didn't say yes,

22
00:01:01,602 --> 00:01:03,645
and now you think you may
have lost her love forever.

23
00:01:03,813 --> 00:01:07,608
How does this compare to me being
forced to relax for a few days?

24
00:01:09,652 --> 00:01:11,987
-It doesn't!
-Thank you!

25
00:01:14,073 --> 00:01:15,532
I'm gonna go talk to Penny.

26
00:01:15,700 --> 00:01:18,869
I'm going to go inside,
put on my coziest pajamas,

27
00:01:19,036 --> 00:01:22,581
curl up with a good book and wait
for this nightmare to be over.

28
00:01:23,165 --> 00:01:25,000
(EXHALES)

29
00:01:26,627 --> 00:01:28,337
Penny.

30
00:01:34,176 --> 00:01:35,385
Sorry.

31
00:01:37,638 --> 00:01:38,680
-Hi.
-Hey.

32
00:01:38,848 --> 00:01:40,140
Look, I'm sorry I
didn't text you back.

33
00:01:40,308 --> 00:01:41,642
I just needed
some time to think.

34
00:01:41,809 --> 00:01:43,852
-Okay.
-Here. Come in.

35
00:01:44,020 --> 00:01:45,896
Look, if you want
to break up, just say it.

36
00:01:46,063 --> 00:01:47,355
-Leonard--
-No, no, no. I take it back.

37
00:01:47,523 --> 00:01:49,441
Don't say it.
Just hate me, but stay with me.

38
00:01:49,609 --> 00:01:51,319
It worked for my parents.

39
00:01:53,487 --> 00:01:56,114
Listen, I don't want
to break up with you.

40
00:01:56,866 --> 00:01:58,367
Oh. Okay.

41
00:01:59,201 --> 00:02:00,535
Good, good.

42
00:02:00,703 --> 00:02:02,871
So it's cool if I cry a little?

43
00:02:04,540 --> 00:02:07,709
-Yeah, I probably wouldn't.
-Yeah.

44
00:02:10,212 --> 00:02:12,923
Look, you did the right thing
last night. I was a mess.

45
00:02:13,090 --> 00:02:15,258
I was just frustrated because
my career is going nowhere.

46
00:02:15,426 --> 00:02:17,219
Look, I get it,
and I want you to know

47
00:02:17,386 --> 00:02:19,888
that I support
whatever you want to do.

48
00:02:20,056 --> 00:02:21,932
Great, because
I've been thinking,

49
00:02:22,099 --> 00:02:23,433
if I really want this
acting thing to work,

50
00:02:23,601 --> 00:02:26,312
I need to focus all my energy on it.
And to do that,

51
00:02:26,479 --> 00:02:29,523
I should quit waitressing
at The Cheesecake Factory.

52
00:02:30,608 --> 00:02:31,400
Wow.

53
00:02:31,567 --> 00:02:33,402
-That's a big step.
- I know.

54
00:02:33,569 --> 00:02:35,696
So, you know, before
making any rash--

55
00:02:35,863 --> 00:02:37,865
- I already quit.
-And I support you.

56
00:02:39,742 --> 00:02:42,327
J (THEME SONG) 7

57
00:03:05,351 --> 00:03:07,102
Come on, take me
to work with you.

58
00:03:07,269 --> 00:03:09,104
No. You're on vacation.

59
00:03:09,271 --> 00:03:11,731
Please? What if there's a big
breakthrough in science today

60
00:03:11,899 --> 00:03:13,066
and I'm not there to see it?

61
00:03:13,234 --> 00:03:14,485
Do you really think
there's gonna be a breakthrough

62
00:03:14,652 --> 00:03:18,030
-without you there to do it?
-No. I was just tricking you.

63
00:03:19,323 --> 00:03:20,782
Bye.

64
00:03:22,702 --> 00:03:24,120
Leonard, wait!

65
00:03:24,286 --> 00:03:26,246
-Take me with you.
-No!

66
00:03:27,039 --> 00:03:28,457
-Please.
-No!

67
00:03:28,624 --> 00:03:30,626
-Too bad. I'm coming with you.
-Sheldon, stay!

68
00:03:30,793 --> 00:03:32,586
-But--
- I said stay!

69
00:03:40,136 --> 00:03:41,804
I'm going to work.

70
00:03:41,971 --> 00:03:43,263
Do not follow me.

71
00:03:53,691 --> 00:03:55,442
(WHIMPERS)

72
00:03:58,988 --> 00:04:00,531
(SIGHS)

73
00:04:02,783 --> 00:04:03,950
BERNADETTE: Hey, Stuart.

74
00:04:05,494 --> 00:04:07,621
-Hey.
-Sorry. Did I startle you?

75
00:04:07,788 --> 00:04:11,124
Yes, but at this point, pretty
much any customer does.

76
00:04:12,001 --> 00:04:14,503
-What can I do for you?
-Well, I need a little help.

77
00:04:14,670 --> 00:04:17,255
I accidentally destroyed one of
Howard's comic books this morning,

78
00:04:17,423 --> 00:04:20,008
-and was hoping I could replace it.
-Wow. What happened?

79
00:04:20,176 --> 00:04:22,845
Batman got his ass kicked
by my curling iron.

80
00:04:24,847 --> 00:04:27,099
Don't let The Riddler know that.

81
00:04:28,768 --> 00:04:30,936
It's a comic book joke.

82
00:04:32,271 --> 00:04:34,189
Or maybe it's not.

83
00:04:35,149 --> 00:04:38,110
-Do you have this one?
-Well, it's pretty rare.

84
00:04:38,277 --> 00:04:40,320
Can you give me a few
days to track it down?

85
00:04:40,488 --> 00:04:43,365
I was kind of hoping to get it
before Howie comes home from work.

86
00:04:43,532 --> 00:04:45,283
-What's the hurry?
-Well, he's always saying

87
00:04:45,451 --> 00:04:47,453
I should be more careful
with my curling iron,

88
00:04:47,620 --> 00:04:48,954
and it seems like
a dangerous precedent

89
00:04:49,121 --> 00:04:51,331
to let him think he can be right.

90
00:04:52,541 --> 00:04:55,794
Well, I'll do what I can,
but I can't make any promises.

91
00:04:56,670 --> 00:05:00,507
You know, I do work
at a pharmaceutical company.

92
00:05:00,674 --> 00:05:02,425
If you can make this happen today,

93
00:05:02,593 --> 00:05:06,138
I can hook you up with anxiety
medication, antidepressants.

94
00:05:06,305 --> 00:05:07,723
Really.

95
00:05:08,724 --> 00:05:10,809
Do you have any of these?

96
00:05:15,731 --> 00:05:18,108
Hello, Mr. Rat Brain.

97
00:05:19,318 --> 00:05:23,280
Not so bitey without the rest of the
rat to back us up now, are we?

98
00:05:23,572 --> 00:05:25,240
-(TAPS ON DOOR)
-Anybody home?

99
00:05:25,491 --> 00:05:26,700
Hey, what brings you guys here?

100
00:05:26,867 --> 00:05:28,285
Well, we were just on our way
to lunch and wanted to see

101
00:05:28,452 --> 00:05:30,579
-if you'd like to join.
-Why?

102
00:05:30,746 --> 00:05:32,164
Because Sheldon's
not here this week,

103
00:05:32,331 --> 00:05:33,749
and you don't think I
have any other options?

104
00:05:33,916 --> 00:05:35,584
I'm just kidding.
I'll get my purse.

105
00:05:36,085 --> 00:05:38,420
Hi, Amy. I... Oh.

106
00:05:38,587 --> 00:05:40,338
I'm sorry. I didn't know
you had any company.

107
00:05:40,506 --> 00:05:43,050
That's okay.
Bert, this is Howard and Rajesh.

108
00:05:43,217 --> 00:05:44,259
Guys, this is Bert.

109
00:05:44,426 --> 00:05:45,427
-Hey. Good to see you.
-Hey.

110
00:05:45,594 --> 00:05:47,137
Anyway, I wanted to show you

111
00:05:47,304 --> 00:05:49,347
this tourmalinated quartz
that we got in the lab.

112
00:05:49,974 --> 00:05:51,266
This is so pretty.

113
00:05:51,433 --> 00:05:52,976
Bert works for the
geology department.

114
00:05:53,143 --> 00:05:56,938
Yeah. You know what geologists
and Bon Jovi have in common?

115
00:05:57,648 --> 00:05:59,483
You're both into rock?

116
00:06:01,527 --> 00:06:03,195
Yeah.

117
00:06:04,864 --> 00:06:08,367
-Well, see ya.
-You forgot your quartz.

118
00:06:09,118 --> 00:06:11,745
Oh, it's okay.
I want you to have it.

119
00:06:12,872 --> 00:06:14,248
Bye.

120
00:06:14,832 --> 00:06:16,041
He's nice.

121
00:06:16,208 --> 00:06:18,919
Yeah, he's nice
because he likes you.

122
00:06:19,086 --> 00:06:20,462
What?

123
00:06:20,629 --> 00:06:23,214
-No, he doesn't.
-He brought you a pretty rock.

124
00:06:23,382 --> 00:06:25,550
So? He does that every day--
Oh.

125
00:06:28,012 --> 00:06:29,221
You know, if you'd
rather skip lunch

126
00:06:29,388 --> 00:06:31,765
and hang out with your boyfriend,
Bert, it's totally okay.

127
00:06:31,932 --> 00:06:33,266
He's not my boyfriend.

128
00:06:33,434 --> 00:06:35,185
Are you sure?
He's tall, pale and awkward.

129
00:06:35,352 --> 00:06:37,645
That sounds like your type.

130
00:06:38,105 --> 00:06:40,816
Should someone as lonely as you
really be making fun of me?

131
00:06:40,983 --> 00:06:42,651
Yeah, grow up, Howard. God.

132
00:06:44,528 --> 00:06:47,113
What do I do?
I don't want to hurt his feelings.

133
00:06:47,281 --> 00:06:49,658
Maybe the problem is
he thinks you're available.

134
00:06:49,825 --> 00:06:51,201
Does he know
you're dating Sheldon?

135
00:06:51,368 --> 00:06:53,536
I guess it hasn't come up.

136
00:06:53,704 --> 00:06:55,580
There you go.

137
00:06:55,748 --> 00:06:58,250
And does Sheldon know
you're dating Sheldon?

138
00:07:00,836 --> 00:07:02,671
I'm sorry. Who are you dating?

139
00:07:03,589 --> 00:07:05,591
Yeah, knock it off, Howard!

140
00:07:15,017 --> 00:07:17,978
-Oh, hey, Sheldon.
-(DEJECTEDLY) Hello.

141
00:07:25,069 --> 00:07:26,653
You okay?

142
00:07:26,820 --> 00:07:29,489
I'm on vacation.
What do you think?

143
00:07:31,033 --> 00:07:32,617
Why are you sitting
in the stairwell?

144
00:07:33,744 --> 00:07:35,746
Leonard told me to stay.

145
00:07:36,830 --> 00:07:38,206
Oh.

146
00:07:38,457 --> 00:07:40,459
Well, good boy.

147
00:07:41,669 --> 00:07:43,712
-Where are you going?
- I have a ton of errands to run.

148
00:07:43,879 --> 00:07:45,922
I need to make copies of my
headshot, send them off to agents

149
00:07:46,090 --> 00:07:47,841
and sign up for a new
acting class.

150
00:07:48,008 --> 00:07:51,011
-Well, have fun.
-Okay.

151
00:07:51,720 --> 00:07:53,388
(WHIMPERS SOFTLY)

152
00:07:57,685 --> 00:07:59,853
-You want to come with me?
-Really?

153
00:08:00,896 --> 00:08:03,315
Come on, boy. Come on.
Let's go. Let's go.

154
00:08:03,482 --> 00:08:05,066
Get in the car. Come on.

155
00:08:07,736 --> 00:08:09,696
All right, thanks a lot.

156
00:08:10,447 --> 00:08:11,990
They have one at Capital Comics.

157
00:08:12,157 --> 00:08:15,827
-That's great.
-No, it's not. I hate that place.

158
00:08:15,995 --> 00:08:17,830
Guy who owns it is a jerk.

159
00:08:17,997 --> 00:08:19,832
He's always making me
feel bad about myself.

160
00:08:19,999 --> 00:08:22,001
That's terrible.

161
00:08:22,751 --> 00:08:24,419
What's the address?

162
00:08:25,879 --> 00:08:26,963
You know, why don't I
just take you there?

163
00:08:27,131 --> 00:08:28,715
That way, I can make sure
he doesn't rip you off.

164
00:08:28,882 --> 00:08:30,717
Thanks, but I don't
want you to close up.

165
00:08:30,884 --> 00:08:32,927
I mean, won't you lose business?

166
00:08:35,681 --> 00:08:37,766
Sorry. That was mean.

167
00:08:41,103 --> 00:08:42,687
Penny really quit
The Cheesecake Factory?

168
00:08:42,855 --> 00:08:44,898
-Yeah.
-So what is she doing today?

169
00:08:45,065 --> 00:08:47,192
I don't know. She already
thinks I don't support this,

170
00:08:47,359 --> 00:08:49,778
so if I call, it might look like
I'm checking up on her.

171
00:08:49,945 --> 00:08:52,072
-Well, do you support this?
-Of course I do.

172
00:08:52,239 --> 00:08:55,450
She's a great actress.
I'm proud she's taking this risk.

173
00:08:55,617 --> 00:08:59,078
-That's nice.
-You bought that? Great!

174
00:09:01,707 --> 00:09:04,167
I got to call her before
I forget how I said it.

175
00:09:06,003 --> 00:09:07,004
Hey.

176
00:09:07,171 --> 00:09:08,964
-Hi. What's up?
-How's it going?

177
00:09:09,131 --> 00:09:10,423
You taking Hollywood by storm?

178
00:09:10,591 --> 00:09:11,925
Actually,
I'm at The Cheesecake Factory.

179
00:09:12,092 --> 00:09:14,427
You got your job back.
That is great news.

180
00:09:14,595 --> 00:09:17,514
I didn't want to say anything,
but you are making the right choice.

181
00:09:17,681 --> 00:09:20,475
To plunge yourself into debt right
now would be literally insane.

182
00:09:20,642 --> 00:09:23,186
Yeah. I'm just
returning my uniform.

183
00:09:25,898 --> 00:09:27,983
And I support you.

184
00:09:34,490 --> 00:09:36,992
MAN: Before we begin your
guided meditation,

185
00:09:37,159 --> 00:09:40,745
close your eyes and picture
yourself in a peaceful environment.

186
00:09:41,538 --> 00:09:42,997
Okay.

187
00:09:44,374 --> 00:09:48,002
I'm inside the CERN super collider.

188
00:09:49,546 --> 00:09:52,674
Now, take a deep, relaxing
breath in through your nose.

189
00:09:55,052 --> 00:09:56,845
And let it out.

190
00:09:57,012 --> 00:09:59,097
Wow. Didn't see that coming.

191
00:10:01,016 --> 00:10:02,183
In.

192
00:10:04,269 --> 00:10:05,353
Let me guess.

193
00:10:05,521 --> 00:10:07,189
And out.

194
00:10:08,607 --> 00:10:10,650
What was I gonna do?
Two "ins" in a row?

195
00:10:10,776 --> 00:10:12,110
(CAR DOOR OPENS)

196
00:10:15,614 --> 00:10:18,199
-Where's my lemonade?
- I didn't get it.

197
00:10:18,367 --> 00:10:21,370
A fitting swan song
to your career as a waitress

198
00:10:21,537 --> 00:10:24,206
to forget my order one last time.

199
00:10:30,379 --> 00:10:32,881
Do you think quitting
my job was a mistake?

200
00:10:33,882 --> 00:10:35,884
Do you see me drinking lemonade?

201
00:10:37,010 --> 00:10:38,386
No. I'm serious.

202
00:10:39,304 --> 00:10:40,722
Why do you ask?

203
00:10:40,889 --> 00:10:43,433
Because Leonard just pissed me off.

204
00:10:43,600 --> 00:10:45,059
Am I being an idiot or not?

205
00:10:45,227 --> 00:10:47,520
No, I don't think you are.

206
00:10:47,688 --> 00:10:49,064
Really?

207
00:10:49,565 --> 00:10:52,526
The best way to achieve
a goal is to devote 100 percent

208
00:10:52,693 --> 00:10:54,653
of your time and energy to it.

209
00:10:54,903 --> 00:10:56,321
When I decided I was
going to be a physicist,

210
00:10:56,488 --> 00:10:59,741
I didn't take some other job
in case it didn't work out.

211
00:10:59,908 --> 00:11:01,910
Which wasn't easy because
there was a lot of pressure

212
00:11:02,077 --> 00:11:04,954
from Ms. Pierson for me
to be chalk monitor that year.

213
00:11:07,249 --> 00:11:09,084
Thank you.
I needed to hear that.

214
00:11:09,251 --> 00:11:11,086
Why can't Leonard understand it?

215
00:11:12,296 --> 00:11:14,840
Because he's not like us, Penny.

216
00:11:15,674 --> 00:11:17,634
We're dreamers.

217
00:11:19,511 --> 00:11:22,597
Yeah, I need to start cracking the
window when I leave you in the car.

218
00:11:29,980 --> 00:11:30,939
Hey.

219
00:11:31,106 --> 00:11:32,440
Hello, Bert.

220
00:11:32,608 --> 00:11:35,402
So, anyway, there's this big
rock and mineral show

221
00:11:35,569 --> 00:11:37,320
next week in Santa Monica and--

222
00:11:37,487 --> 00:11:41,115
Listen... Bert, before you
say anything else, |I...

223
00:11:41,867 --> 00:11:43,410
I have a boyfriend.

224
00:11:43,619 --> 00:11:46,455
Oh. This is awkward.

225
00:11:46,622 --> 00:11:49,541
You thought I was gonna ask you
to go with me to the mineral show.

226
00:11:49,708 --> 00:11:50,875
Weren't you?

227
00:11:52,002 --> 00:11:53,628
Yeah.

228
00:11:56,089 --> 00:11:59,967
That's very nice of you,
but I do have a boyfriend.

229
00:12:00,135 --> 00:12:01,553
That's what you all say.

230
00:12:01,720 --> 00:12:02,721
You just don't want
to go out with me

231
00:12:02,888 --> 00:12:04,890
because I have
an off-putting personality.

232
00:12:05,057 --> 00:12:06,641
No, that's not true.

233
00:12:06,808 --> 00:12:08,810
My boyfriend has
an off-putting personality, too.

234
00:12:08,977 --> 00:12:11,187
Way worse than you.

235
00:12:13,315 --> 00:12:15,483
Don't worry. I'm used to it.

236
00:12:15,651 --> 00:12:18,570
I mean, I'm big and weird
and funny-looking

237
00:12:18,737 --> 00:12:21,448
and no one ever wants
to do anything with me.

238
00:12:22,032 --> 00:12:23,825
Don't say that.

239
00:12:24,243 --> 00:12:27,204
It's okay.
I know I'm a monster.

240
00:12:27,371 --> 00:12:29,664
No, Bert, come on.

241
00:12:30,624 --> 00:12:32,334
I'd love to go to the
mineral show with you.

242
00:12:32,501 --> 00:12:35,170
Sweet. It's a date.

243
00:12:38,423 --> 00:12:40,842
-No, it's not.
-BERT: Too late!

244
00:12:48,850 --> 00:12:51,060
Wow.

245
00:12:52,688 --> 00:12:55,065
Yeah. Haven't seen this
many people in my store

246
00:12:55,232 --> 00:12:58,693
since that Korean church bus
crashed through my front window.

247
00:12:59,778 --> 00:13:02,405
-Hey! Stuart!
-Jesse.

248
00:13:02,572 --> 00:13:05,700
Haven't seen you in forever.
Look how gray you've gotten.

249
00:13:05,867 --> 00:13:08,202
My hair's exactly
the same color as always.

250
00:13:08,370 --> 00:13:10,455
No, I was talking about your skin.

251
00:13:11,873 --> 00:13:13,958
Look... my friend here
needs a comic book--

252
00:13:14,167 --> 00:13:16,377
Ooh! And she went into
your store by mistake.

253
00:13:16,962 --> 00:13:19,130
Good thing there was no
one there to see you.

254
00:13:19,840 --> 00:13:21,174
What do you need?

255
00:13:21,842 --> 00:13:24,803
Oh, yeah, yeah. I got this.
Right over here.

256
00:13:27,306 --> 00:13:29,057
Even you, Sweatpants?

257
00:13:29,224 --> 00:13:30,975
Free popcorn.

258
00:13:32,644 --> 00:13:34,312
Can I offer you a coffee?

259
00:13:34,479 --> 00:13:36,814
-Espresso? Latte?
-No, thanks.

260
00:13:36,982 --> 00:13:38,775
How about you, Stu?
Mocha? Scone?

261
00:13:38,942 --> 00:13:41,235
Directions to the
nearest soup kitchen?

262
00:13:42,446 --> 00:13:43,905
-Hey.
-I'm just kidding.

263
00:13:44,072 --> 00:13:46,240
He knows where the soup kitchen is.

264
00:13:48,744 --> 00:13:50,287
It's on Merton Avenue.

265
00:13:51,872 --> 00:13:54,165
I don't think I like the way
you're treating my friend.

266
00:13:54,333 --> 00:13:55,792
Sorry.

267
00:13:55,959 --> 00:13:58,169
-You want the book or not?
-Not from you.

268
00:13:58,879 --> 00:14:00,422
Let's go, Stuart.

269
00:14:03,550 --> 00:14:05,593
You know something, Jesse?

270
00:14:05,761 --> 00:14:07,596
You may have a
successful business

271
00:14:07,763 --> 00:14:11,099
and the kind of pink complexion
that comes with good nutrition...

272
00:14:12,601 --> 00:14:14,603
but I have something
more important.

273
00:14:14,770 --> 00:14:18,023
-What's that?
-Friendship.

274
00:14:21,276 --> 00:14:24,070
Which I would trade in a
heartbeat for all of this.

275
00:14:27,449 --> 00:14:29,451
The mineral and rock show?

276
00:14:29,618 --> 00:14:32,329
That would be awful even
without Bert.

277
00:14:33,455 --> 00:14:35,457
So what am I supposed to do now?

278
00:14:35,624 --> 00:14:38,877
Prepare your uterus
for his gigantic offspring?

279
00:14:41,129 --> 00:14:42,797
This isn't funny.

280
00:14:42,964 --> 00:14:44,256
I'm gonna have to
tell him the truth:

281
00:14:44,424 --> 00:14:45,800
that even if I didn't
have a boyfriend,

282
00:14:45,967 --> 00:14:47,468
I wouldn't be interested in him.

283
00:14:47,636 --> 00:14:49,638
I've heard those
words so many times.

284
00:14:49,805 --> 00:14:51,932
From Linda Nosenchuck,
Tammy Rosenworcel...

285
00:14:52,099 --> 00:14:53,475
Padma Kapur, Neha Chowdury...

286
00:14:53,642 --> 00:14:55,477
Marci Grossman,
Lisa Mazzarino...

287
00:14:55,644 --> 00:14:57,145
-Megan Pincus...
-Tammy Cho...

288
00:14:57,312 --> 00:14:58,646
Who was that girl
from our Starbucks?

289
00:14:58,814 --> 00:15:01,024
-Arlene Russell!
-Yes! Arlene!

290
00:15:02,025 --> 00:15:05,194
She wrote "no way"
on both our cappuccinos.

291
00:15:06,780 --> 00:15:08,156
Poor Bert.

292
00:15:08,323 --> 00:15:10,491
That guy's got a rough
afternoon ahead of him.

293
00:15:10,659 --> 00:15:14,287
Well, how would you want a girl
to tell you she wasn't interested?

294
00:15:14,454 --> 00:15:18,954
I guess, uh, I'd like her to sit me
down, look me in the eye and say,

295
00:15:19,626 --> 00:15:22,128
"I was wrong. I love you."

296
00:15:22,295 --> 00:15:25,548
And then maybe she could
touch me in a special way.

297
00:15:27,300 --> 00:15:29,343
That's how you reject a guy.

298
00:15:30,095 --> 00:15:31,221
Okay, I don't have time for this.

299
00:15:31,388 --> 00:15:33,848
I'm just gonna go find him
and be brutally honest.

300
00:15:34,015 --> 00:15:35,349
-No, don't.
-He'll be so upset.

301
00:15:35,517 --> 00:15:37,310
He'll probably climb
up the Empire State Building

302
00:15:37,477 --> 00:15:39,520
and start swatting at planes.

303
00:15:44,401 --> 00:15:45,777
You want us to talk to him?

304
00:15:45,944 --> 00:15:47,987
Really? You would do that?

305
00:15:48,155 --> 00:15:49,865
Sure. We've both been in his shoes.

306
00:15:50,031 --> 00:15:52,366
We'll let him down with
compassion and respect.

307
00:15:53,285 --> 00:15:55,495
-Thank you.
-Let's go.

308
00:15:58,039 --> 00:15:59,040
So we tell him
she's a lesbian, right?

309
00:15:59,207 --> 00:16:01,209
Of course we tell him
she's a lesbian.

310
00:16:09,593 --> 00:16:11,928
And hold three...

311
00:16:12,095 --> 00:16:14,514
two... one.

312
00:16:14,681 --> 00:16:15,682
Very good.

313
00:16:17,100 --> 00:16:19,435
Now let's try Warrior.

314
00:16:20,854 --> 00:16:22,438
And hold.

315
00:16:25,734 --> 00:16:29,070
I've read that there are great
yogis who have such mastery

316
00:16:29,237 --> 00:16:33,157
over their bodies they can draw
water in through their genitals.

317
00:16:41,791 --> 00:16:44,585
Yeah, well, I don't think we're
gonna get to do that today.

318
00:16:46,213 --> 00:16:47,714
Too bad.

319
00:16:47,881 --> 00:16:49,716
It seems like a good way
to drink a milk shake

320
00:16:49,883 --> 00:16:51,926
without getting brain freeze.

321
00:16:54,513 --> 00:16:55,931
Oh, hey.

322
00:16:56,097 --> 00:16:57,765
And now we go to Reverse Warrior.

323
00:17:03,688 --> 00:17:05,272
How did she get you to do yoga?

324
00:17:05,857 --> 00:17:09,193
Well, to be honest,
I thought she said "Yoda."

325
00:17:12,447 --> 00:17:16,367
I'm helping him relax because,
unlike you, he supports me.

326
00:17:16,660 --> 00:17:18,953
Oh, How many times
do I have to say it?

327
00:17:19,120 --> 00:17:21,455
- I support you.
-Sheldon, take a break.

328
00:17:22,999 --> 00:17:24,667
Namaste.

329
00:17:26,169 --> 00:17:28,713
Okay, if you support me,
what was with that phone call?

330
00:17:28,880 --> 00:17:31,507
Fine. I'm not sure
you should have quit.

331
00:17:31,675 --> 00:17:33,134
But if you care so
much what I think,

332
00:17:33,301 --> 00:17:34,760
why didn't you ask me
before you did it?

333
00:17:34,928 --> 00:17:36,262
Oh, so now I need
your permission?

334
00:17:36,429 --> 00:17:38,305
Would you have asked me
before you quit your job?

335
00:17:38,473 --> 00:17:40,975
Yes. I thought we were
in the kind of relationship

336
00:17:41,142 --> 00:17:42,810
where we make decisions together.

337
00:17:42,978 --> 00:17:44,354
If I'm wrong,
then maybe we need to talk

338
00:17:44,521 --> 00:17:46,147
about the kind of relationship
we're actually in.

339
00:17:46,314 --> 00:17:47,648
Yeah, well, maybe we do.

340
00:17:47,816 --> 00:17:49,651
I'm willing to if you guys are.

341
00:17:51,736 --> 00:17:52,820
Can we please
have some privacy?

342
00:17:52,988 --> 00:17:54,322
No.

343
00:17:54,489 --> 00:17:56,324
I'm as much a part of this
relationship as you two,

344
00:17:56,491 --> 00:17:59,118
and I think it's high time we
put all our cards on the table.

345
00:17:59,286 --> 00:18:01,413
Yeah. For example,
where is this going?

346
00:18:01,580 --> 00:18:03,415
Are you two ever getting married?

347
00:18:03,582 --> 00:18:07,127
And, if so, where will we all live?
Have you thought about that?

348
00:18:08,670 --> 00:18:10,004
-No.
-Penny?

349
00:18:10,171 --> 00:18:11,505
OK, wait. What are we doing?

350
00:18:11,673 --> 00:18:13,341
For some reason,
we're planning a future

351
00:18:13,508 --> 00:18:15,635
where we both live
with Sheldon forever.

352
00:18:15,802 --> 00:18:17,762
Good. Now we're getting somewhere.

353
00:18:19,389 --> 00:18:21,724
Look, I know you think I'm being
reckless, and you might be right,

354
00:18:21,891 --> 00:18:23,309
but I need to take this shot.

355
00:18:23,476 --> 00:18:27,521
No kidding. Despite what it says
on her résumé, she is no longer 22.

356
00:18:31,651 --> 00:18:33,944
I swear, I am on your side.

357
00:18:34,112 --> 00:18:36,989
You keep saying you're on my
side, but you don't act like it.

358
00:18:37,157 --> 00:18:39,534
He does that to me, too.
Why do we put up with it?

359
00:18:41,703 --> 00:18:44,914
Listen, I could never do
what you're doing, okay?

360
00:18:45,081 --> 00:18:47,625
-I would be terrified.
-Well, it's scary for me, too.

361
00:18:47,792 --> 00:18:49,627
I'm fine with it.

362
00:18:50,920 --> 00:18:55,049
My point is, just because I couldn't
do it doesn't mean you shouldn't.

363
00:18:55,216 --> 00:18:57,635
And I'm proud of you.

364
00:18:59,596 --> 00:19:02,223
Okay. Thank you.

365
00:19:02,682 --> 00:19:04,558
Well, to celebrate
this reconciliation,

366
00:19:04,726 --> 00:19:06,269
let's all share a milk shake.

367
00:19:06,436 --> 00:19:08,980
Penny, you'll need a straw.

368
00:19:15,403 --> 00:19:16,904
-You're back.
-Yes, I am!

369
00:19:17,072 --> 00:19:18,531
There's a few more things
I want to say to you.

370
00:19:18,698 --> 00:19:21,701
Stuart's store is just fine, and he's
a much nicer person than you are,

371
00:19:21,868 --> 00:19:24,453
and if you still have that comic,
I'd like to buy it right now!

372
00:19:25,872 --> 00:19:27,039
No problem.

373
00:19:27,207 --> 00:19:29,584
Oh, you want a latte
while you wait?

374
00:19:29,751 --> 00:19:31,586
No, I don't want a latte!

375
00:19:31,753 --> 00:19:34,505
I want a cappuccino
and a blueberry scone!

376
00:19:35,256 --> 00:19:39,009
- I only have chocolate chip.
-Well, that sounds even better!

377
00:19:45,266 --> 00:19:48,185
Thanks for coming to the
mineral and rock show with me.

378
00:19:52,232 --> 00:19:54,776
We're sorry Amy didn't want to go.

379
00:19:54,943 --> 00:19:57,737
Really, really sorry.

380
00:19:58,905 --> 00:20:01,741
Nah, who needs her
when I have you guys?

381
00:20:01,908 --> 00:20:05,453
CHANTING: Rock show!
Rock show! Rock show!

382
00:20:05,912 --> 00:20:07,747
Rock show! Rock show!

383
00:20:07,914 --> 00:20:12,414
Rock show!
Rock show!

384
00:20:18,007 --> 00:20:21,135
s (THEME MUSIC) &

385
00:20:38,236 --> 00:20:40,238
(English - SDH)

